## Complexity Analysis

Let d be the number of digits in x.

Each digit is processed exactly once.

Time Complexity:

O(d)

Since:

d = O(log |x|)

we can also express the complexity as:

O(log |x|)

Because x is restricted to a signed 32-bit integer, it contains at most 10 digits. Therefore, under the fixed problem constraints, the number of iterations is bounded by a constant.

Auxiliary Space:

O(1)

Only a constant number of variables are used.

No array, list, set, string, or other growing data structure is required.

